11. identityMatchesSuppressed handles BOTH stored key forms (stable_id.go:41):
    `key == t.StableID` when StableID non-empty, then `key == t.Hash` — so a
    decision holding a StableID (post-A1) OR a legacy hash (pre-A1 decision
    or a row outside the loaded set) both match correctly.

12. coverage_test.go change (TestBuildPageData_PinnedHashesReachSummary)
    replaces `pins[hash] == ""` with `dl.PinFor(ts.Transactions[0])`. The
    old assertion encoded the pre-A1 key convention (direct hash index into
    the pins map); behavior 3 (rekey on save) invalidates that convention,
    so the change is the legitimate reason to edit a pre-existing test, not
    papering over a regression. PinFor resolves either key form, so the test
    still discriminates a real regression (a missing pin returns ok=false).

